      "claim": "Bupropion showed rapid equilibration across the BBB with a Kp,uu of 1.9, demonstrating active and meaningful unbound brain exposure.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C10"],
      "claim": "Clevidipine was found at significantly high brain levels shortly after dosing with a high Kp, confirming its ability to cross the BBB.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "All retrieved experimental evidence, with uniformly high assay-transfer scores, supports BBB permeability and meaningful CNS access. Multiple direct in vivo measurements—PET brain uptake, CSF/plasma ratios, Kp,uu, and brain tissue distribution—consistently indicate that the query molecule is likely to achieve adequate CNS exposure after systemic administration.",
